	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(321.4285714285715, 83.57142857142856, 150.0, 34.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Ground truth</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(460.0, 214.99999999999994, 150.0, 144.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Drops name + host name (causes encoding-based errors)
Also sets ID as meta</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/plain" rect="(656.883116883117, 5.000000000000028, 464.5454545454544, 103.27272727272727)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">This procressing chain first discretizes to 10 equal bins (roughly 10th percentiles), then only selecting the highest bin (&gt;= 90th percentile) and then getting the ID column to query the original dataset</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/plain" rect="(1041.2857142857142, 439.5357142857142, 257.0, 100.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Retrieving by index the properties with the top 10% of reviews</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/plain" rect="(1350.0, 436.25, 265.0, 100.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Returning count of properties in Chch city (343 as of current count)</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/plain" rect="(1292.5, 183.75, 150.0, 56.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">Histogram by region (bonus!)</text>
	</annotations>
